    "body": "### Expected behavior\n\nI was trying to figure out good settings for batch size and bulk size when using the Loader API to insert a large number of rows into a table.\r\n\r\nI expected that all passed rows will be inserted into the table, or that an Exception is thrown.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nWith some settings, all rows were added to the table. In other cases, none (0, null) rows were inserted, but the code just continued normally.\n\n### Steps to reproduce the problem\n\nCreate a PostgreSQL database with the following table:\r\n\r\n```sql\r\nCREATE TABLE Link\r\n(\r\n\tid       BIGINT        NOT NULL UNIQUE, -- deliberately no auto-increment\r\n\tlinkId   VARCHAR(1000) NOT NULL,\r\n\tgeometry TEXT          NOT NULL\r\n);\r\n\r\nCREATE INDEX Link_linkId ON Link (linkId);\r\n```\r\n\r\nRun the following Java code:\r\n```java\r\nimport com.example.db.jooq.tables.records.LinkRecord;\r\nimport org.jooq.DSLContext;\r\nimport org.jooq.SQLDialect;\r\nimport org.jooq.conf.RenderNameCase;\r\nimport org.jooq.conf.Settings;\r\nimport org.jooq.impl.DSL;\r\n\r\nimport java.io.IOException;\r\nimport java.sql.Connection;\r\nimport java.sql.DriverManager;\r\nimport java.sql.SQLException;\r\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\r\nimport java.util.List;\r\nimport java.util.function.Supplier;\r\n\r\nimport static com.example.db.jooq.tables.Link.LINK;\r\n\r\npublic class JooqDebug {\r\n\r\n\tprivate static final long COUNT = 100_000;\r\n\r\n\tpublic static void main(String[] args) throws SQLException {\r\n\r\n\t\tString connectionString = \"jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/test-db\";\r\n\r\n\t\tConnection conn = DriverManager.getConnection(connectionString, \"postgres\", \"****\");\r\n\r\n\t\tvar jooqSettings = new Settings();\r\n\t\tjooqSettings.setRenderNameCase(RenderNameCase.LOWER);\r\n\r\n\t\tSupplier<DSLContext> cp = () -> DSL.using(conn, SQLDialect.POSTGRES, jooqSettings);\r\n\r\n\t\tjooqLoader(cp.get(), 20_000, 20_000);\r\n\t\tjooqLoader(cp.get(), 25_000, 20_000);\r\n\t\tjooqLoader(cp.get(), 25_000, 25_000);\r\n\t\tjooqLoader(cp.get(), 20_000, 25_000);\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n\tpublic static void jooqLoader(DSLContext c, int batchSize, int bulkSize) {\r\n\t\tc.dsl().deleteFrom(LINK).execute();\r\n\r\n\t\tList<LinkRecord> rows = new ArrayList<>(batchSize);\r\n\t\tfor (long i = 0; i < COUNT; i++) {\r\n\t\t\trows.add(new LinkRecord(i, \"link\" + i, \"geometry\" + i));\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tc.dsl().transaction(ctx -> {\r\n\t\t\ttry {\r\n\t\t\t\tctx.dsl()\r\n\t\t\t\t\t.loadInto(LINK)\r\n\t\t\t\t\t.batchAfter(batchSize)\r\n\t\t\t\t\t.bulkAfter(bulkSize)\r\n\t\t\t\t\t.commitAfter(1)\r\n\t\t\t\t\t.onErrorAbort()\r\n\t\t\t\t\t.loadRecords(rows)\r\n\t\t\t\t\t.fields(LINK.ID, LINK.LINKID, LINK.GEOMETRY)\r\n\t\t\t\t\t.execute();\r\n\t\t\t} catch (IOException e) {\r\n\t\t\t\te.printStackTrace();\r\n\t\t\t\tthrow new RuntimeException(e);\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t});\r\n\r\n\t\tSystem.out.println(c.dsl().fetchCount(LINK));\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nYes, the actual numbers (25k for bulkSize and batchSize) might not make sense, but I would still expect some Exception and not just 0 rows.\n\n### jOOQ Version\n\njOOQ OpenSource 3.18.2, and also 3.17.8\n\n### Database product and version\n\nPostgreSQL 14.4\n\n### Java Version\n\nEclipse Temurin 17.0.4\n\n### OS Version\n\nmacOS 12.6\n\n### JDBC driver name and version (include name if unofficial driver)\n\norg.postgresql:postgresql:42.5.4",
